    description: "Pass 17 finding CCCCCC. 4001 of 33830 nodes have non-empty modifiers list. Six distinct values: private (3942 python), re_exported (39 python), public (8 csharp+java), exported (6 go), pub (4 rust), external (2 solidity). Five different words for what is semantically 'visibility'. Bundle candidate for the classification_axes ADR alongside s8 VV (edge.type extends/inherits/implements leak) and s16 IIIII (evidence_type vocab fragmentation)."  # ef17
    fields:  # ef17
      statement: "The node.modifiers field should use a single normalized vocabulary across languages; language-specific terms for the same semantic concept (visibility) violate the cross-language axis property."  # ef17
      root_cause: "Each language analyzer emits its own native visibility keyword (csharp/java->'public', rust->'pub', go->'exported', solidity->'external', python->'private'/'re_exported') without normalization to a shared vocabulary."  # ef17
